\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesu, the very thought of Thee
\par With sweetness fills my breast;
\par But sweeter far Thy face to see,
\par And in Thy presence rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Nor voice can sing, nor heart can frame,
\par Nor can the memory find
\par A sweeter sound than Thy blest name,
\par O Saviour of mankind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Hope of every contrite heart,
\par O Joy of all the meek,
\par To those who fall how kind Thou art!
\par How good to those who seek!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. But what to those who find? Ah! this
\par Nor tongue nor pen can show:
\par The love of Jesus, what it is
\par None but His loved ones know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesu, our only joy be Thou,
\par As Thou our prize wilt be;
\par Jesu, be Thou our glory now,
\par And through eternity.
\par                         Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

